  "notes": "Fire Tester 0.1.717b fixes BLE restoration after an AP session by preparing persistent Tone task and display DMA descriptors before releasing the protected BLE heap reserve. It also keeps radio-owned generic allocations in PSRAM, cleans up portal-owned handlers, and corrects the NimBLE host-task teardown handle. The main framebuffer remains INTERNAL and BLE memory admission floors are unchanged.\n\nQR Help opens as an animated child of the notification curtain. Back is focused automatically; physical LEFT returns to the error list, and holding DOWN closes the curtain with its existing progress indicator. The QR remains white on the dark background.\n\nValidation: 32 focused host suites, independent review, checked PlatformIO build, verified USB installation, two real AP/HTTP/cleanup cycles, and subsequent read-only Twin Button observation. Operator flashlight learning is preserved. This does not claim phone RF endurance or complete physical-device QA. The paused charger-control experiment remains paused.",
